documentation and other files, in every version released under this license.

"You" means the person or organization using the Software under this license.

"Unmodified" means exactly as the Licensor released it, with no file added, removed or changed.

"Contribution" means any change, code, documentation or other material that you submit to the
Licensor for inclusion in the Software, for example as a pull request, a patch or an issue.


2. What you may do

Free of charge, worldwide and without time limit, you may:

a. Use the Software for any purpose, personal or commercial. For example, you may edit videos with
   it for yourself, for your employer or for paying clients, and you own the videos you make.

b. Use the engine library in your own software by calling it as it is, including in commercial
   software, as long as the library's files stay Unmodified and the product you offer is not
   substantially the Software itself (see section 3).

c. Make and give away Unmodified copies of the Software, for example by passing the installer to
   someone or offering it on an internal software list, as long as you charge nothing for them and
   each copy includes this license and the Software's copyright notices.

d. Read and study the source code.

e. Fork the repository on GitHub and change your fork only in order to prepare, test and submit
   Contributions to the Licensor's repository. A changed version may not be used for any other
   purpose or passed to anyone except through a Contribution.


3. What you may not do

a. Sell, rent, lease or sublicense the Software, or charge any fee for copies of it, for access to
   it or for permission to use it. This includes offering the Software, or a product that is
   substantially the Software, as a paid app, download, subscription or hosted service.

b. Change the Software, or make, use or distribute a modified version or a work derived from it,
   except as section 2(e) allows for Contributions.

c. Remove or change the copyright notices, this license or the notices of third-party components.

d. Claim to be the author or owner of the Software or of the project, or present the Software or
   any part of it as your own work.

e. Use the names "VideditBridge" or "Moses Henen", or the VideditBridge logo, to name or promote
   your own products, or in a way that suggests the Licensor endorses you, except to say truthfully
   that you use the Software or that you contributed to it.


